## CODING STANDARDS

### UnoCSS Styling
- When applying UnoCSS classes, prioritize readability and maintainability.
- Use descriptive class names that clearly indicate the intended style.
- Ensure consistency in the use of font sizes, weights, colors, and spacing across different elements.
- Consider using the following styles for common HTML elements:
    - `h1`: `text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2` (large font, bold, dark gray, bottom margin)
    - `h2`: `text-lg font-medium text-gray-600 mb-3` (medium font, medium weight, medium gray, bottom margin)
    - `p`: `text-base text-gray-700 leading-relaxed` (base font size, slightly dark gray, relaxed line height)

